## Financial Concepts

### Stationarity

A stationary time series has statistical properties that remain stable over time.

### Log Returns

A standard measure of financial asset performance used in quantitative finance.

### ADF Test

A statistical test used to determine whether a time series is stationary.

### ARIMA

A classical forecasting model designed to capture linear relationships in time series data.

### GARCH

A volatility modeling framework widely used in financial risk management.

### Volatility Clustering

A phenomenon where periods of high volatility tend to be followed by high volatility, and periods of low volatility tend to follow low volatility.

